<!--
  DO NOT build, pack, sign, or add this project to AspNetCore.slnx / any ProjectToBuild list.

  Exists solely so Dependabot can discover and update the external NuGet packages listed in
  eng/Dependencies.props. Real projects reference those packages via <Reference Include="X" />
  (see eng/targets/ResolveReferences.targets, docs/ReferenceResolution.md), an indirection
  Dependabot's MSBuild-based discovery can't see through. This project restates them as literal
  <PackageReference> items using the same eng/Versions.props version properties, so Dependabot
  can find and bump them - bumping a property here updates the real dependency too.

  Keep in sync with eng/Dependencies.props: CodeCheck.ps1 fails if eng/Dependencies.props changes
  without a matching change here. Maestro-managed packages (eng/Version.Details.props) and the
  $(IdentityModelVersion)-pinned IdentityModel packages are intentionally omitted; see
  .github/dependabot.yml for the matching ignore list. See README.md for more details.

  Do NOT set ExcludeFromBuild here: Arcade's ExcludeFromBuild disables NuGet restore entirely
  (points NuGetRestoreTargets at an empty file), which would also stop Dependabot resolving any
  packages out of this project. Nothing globs eng/tools/** into the real build or references this
  project, so it never participates in a real build anyway.

  A few real, referenced packages are intentionally omitted because Dependabot can never treat
  them as updatable no matter how they're declared:
  - NETStandard.Library: dependabot-core hard-codes this as "resolved but not reported" (an SDK
    compatibility shim, not something anyone updates independently).
  - Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers: the .NET SDK implicitly references this itself, so
    MSBuild marks any explicit reference IsImplicitlyDefined="true", which dependabot-core treats
    as non-top-level/non-updatable.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>$(DefaultNetCoreTargetFramework);net472</TargetFrameworks>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsShipping>false</IsShipping>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
    <!--
      Combining ~90 unrelated packages' transitive dependencies in one project triggers NuGet
      "downgrade" conflicts (NU1605) that never occur in their real, separate consuming projects.
      This project is never actually built or consumed, so suppress it instead of chasing every
      transitive constraint.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU1605</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

